{"name":"Whisky Cola","hex":"#772233","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"whisky","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative form of whiskey, an alcoholic liquor distilled from fermented grain, usually aged in oak barrels,  Scotch; a drink of this liquor. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}"]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative form of whiskey (“a light gig or carriage”)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/whisky"},{"term":"cola","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The kola plant, genus Cola, famous for its nut, or one of these nuts.","A beverage or a drink made with kola nut flavoring, caramel and carbonated water."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of colon."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cola"}],"entries":[{"title":"Whisky","blocks":[{"text":"Whisky or whiskey is a type of liquor made from fermented grain mash. Various grains are used for different varieties, including barley, corn, rye, and wheat. Whisky is typically aged in wooden casks, commonly of charred white oak. Uncharred white oak casks previously used for the aging of port, rum, or sherry may be employed during storage to impart a unique flavour and colour."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a2/Whiskyhogmanay2010.jpg/330px-Whiskyhogmanay2010.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Whisky","wikidata":"Q281"},{"title":"Cola","blocks":[{"text":"Cola is a carbonated soft drink flavored with vanilla, cinnamon, citrus oils, and other flavorings. The name, however, comes from the kola nut, which imbues the beverage with the stimulant caffeine. A stimulating soda using kola appeared circa 1880 in the United States."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/Glass_of_Cola.jpg/330px-Glass_of_Cola.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://e